    "updated_at": "2020-11-12T02:28:11Z",
    "body": "Trying out starship for the first time this week. Used `brew` to install it and ran into this issue when trying to run `source ~/.zshrc` after adding the recommended way of `eval “$(starship init zsh)”` to the end of my .zshrc file:\r\n\r\n```\r\n(eval):1: command not found: “source\r\nthread 'main' panicked at 'failed printing to stdout: Broken pipe (os error 32)', library/std/src/io/stdio.rs:895:9                                                                                                                                   \r\nnote: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace\r\n```\r\n\r\nEnded up here and the solution for me was using `eval \"$($(brew --prefix)/bin/starship init zsh)\"` instead. Figured I would share this incase anyone else runs into this problem. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
