    "updated_at": "2021-09-06T17:36:59Z",
    "body": "It looks like we had competing PRs opened on this: #1344 and #1365. #1344 (which is a PR to do this with the `which` crate) has quite a wall of debate that I was apparently moderately involved in, but at the moment I can't remember all the details of what's going on.\r\n\r\nI think part of the problem is that the current init system evolved out of a bunch of use cases and bugs which needed to be solved individually, but we don't have anything written down for what the requirements are. I remember the early days of starship requiring some delicate workarounds for Termux, NixOS, and bash 3.2, but I can't remember what problems we had or why we solved them the way we did.\r\n\r\nI'll see if I can dig through the issues/PRs/blames to figure out exactly what systems we explicitly have support for and what quirks they have, so that we can hopefully merge an updated version of #1344 without worrying about forgetting about an edge case.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
